---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Pillar from "../components/Pillar.astro";
import PanelShot from "../components/PanelShot.astro";
const title = "Sidecar privacy — what leaves your Mac";
const description =
  "Plain-language privacy: your conversation goes only to the assistant you chose, on your own subscription; the developer runs no server; saved chats live on your Mac. Here's exactly what leaves, and what you control.";
---
<Base title={title} description={description} active="privacy">
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy &amp; control</p>
      <h1>You decide what's kept.</h1>
      <p>Sidecar is local-first: it has no server of its own. Your conversation goes only to the AI you already pay for, and everything it remembers lives on your Mac. Here's the honest breakdown.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding-top:16px">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="pillars" style="padding:0 0 12px">
        <Pillar title="Your own subscription">Answers come from Claude or Codex through your sign-in — no extra account, no separate bill, no API key.</Pillar>
        <Pillar title="Nothing to the developer">No server of ours sits in the middle. No analytics, no tracking, no ads. The developer never sees your chats or pages.</Pillar>
        <Pillar title="On your computer">Conversations and settings are stored on your Mac, and searching them happens there too — your search words are never sent anywhere.</Pillar>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><p class="eyebrow">The honest part</p><h2>What actually leaves your Mac.</h2></div>
      <div class="baseline"><b>Always, no setting:</b> the page text you ask about and your words go to the assistant you chose. That's how it answers.</div>
      <div class="outbound" style="margin-bottom:16px">
        <b>Your question and its context</b> — with any page text, file, or transcript you included — go from the extension to the companion app <b>over your own computer</b> (<span class="kbd">127.0.0.1</span>, which never leaves your machine), and from there to <b>the assistant you chose</b>: Claude Code → Anthropic, or Codex → OpenAI, on your own subscription, the same path those tools use themselves.
      </div>
      <div class="outbound" style="margin-bottom:16px">
        <b>A web search</b> — when a question needs current information, your assistant runs one, and (only if you turn on "open live web pages") opens pages during it. That goes through Anthropic or OpenAI on your subscription, not any server of ours.
      </div>
      <div class="outbound">
        <b>The panel's fonts</b> load from Google Fonts — the same web-font fetch any site using Google Fonts makes, with no conversation content. Turning on the natural read-aloud voice or video listening downloads those components once, from a fixed source checked against a known fingerprint — again, no conversation content. A couple of optional, off-by-default features add a few more cases, listed below. Everything else — your saved chats, searching them, reading aloud, and the highlight button — stays on your computer.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><p class="eyebrow">Your switches</p><h2>Everything optional is off by default.</h2><p>Each setting below starts off, and each is explained next to its switch in Settings.</p></div>
      <div class="control-grid">
        <div>
          <div class="tbl-wrap">
            <table>
              <thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>What it does</th><th>Does anything new leave your Mac?</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td>Highlight button</td><td>Shows the "Ask in Sidecar" button on selected text.</td><td class="no">No — not until you click it</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Save the pictures</td><td>Keeps captured/attached images in the saved conversation.</td><td class="no">No — on your Mac</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Remember what I listen to</td><td>Saves the video transcripts you captured.</td><td class="no">No — on your Mac</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Skip the page for general questions</td><td>Decides, on your computer, when a question doesn't need the page.</td><td class="no">No — decided locally</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Let the assistant look at the page</td><td>Lets it grab a screenshot on its own when a question seems visual.</td><td class="yes">The screenshot, to your assistant</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Show pictures from the web</td><td>Finds pictures of what you asked about; on a fresh ask they load right away (a reopened chat waits for "Show previews").</td><td class="yes">Yes — opens web pages, and each preview loads from its website</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Open live web pages</td><td>Lets a search fetch pages for more detail.</td><td class="yes">Yes — via your subscription</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
        <PanelShot src="settings.png" width={1536} height={2560} alt="Sidecar's Settings, where each optional feature lives under its own section." />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><p class="eyebrow">What's kept</p><h2>Saved on your Mac, controlled by you.</h2></div>
      <ul class="kf-points" style="max-width:70ch;grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:12px">
        <li><b>Conversations are saved by default</b> so you can reopen them — your messages, text you brought in (a highlight, an attached file's text), the text of pages you chatted about, the titles of those pages, and a web answer's source links. You can turn saving off in Settings.</li>
        <li><b>Deleting a conversation</b> and <b>"forget this page"</b> (which removes a page's saved text and remembered title) live on the companion app's admin page — open it from <b>Settings → "Open admin page ↗"</b>.</li>
        <li><b>Pictures and audio transcripts</b> are kept only if you switch on their off-by-default settings.</li>
        <li><b>A log file</b> is written only if you set the app to start automatically at login; it lives in the same permission-protected folder (readable only by you) and isn't written when you launch the app yourself.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head"><p class="eyebrow">Never</p><h2>What Sidecar does not do.</h2></div>
      <ul class="kf-points" style="max-width:70ch;grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:12px">
        <li>It does <b>not</b> sell or share your data with anyone.</li>
        <li>It does <b>not</b> use your data for advertising, profiling, or credit decisions.</li>
        <li>It does <b>not</b> send your data to the developer, or to anyone other than the assistant you chose — Anthropic for Claude, OpenAI for Codex — via your own subscription.</li>
        <li>It loads <b>no remote code</b>; all of the extension's code ships inside the extension package.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="kf-note">Questions about privacy: panchaoai@gmail.com. This is a plain-language summary; wording is reviewed against Sidecar 0.1.5.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
